    rdf:value """of a Salon. Her husband is an old scholar, with the old- fashioned simple courtesy  d’antan . He told a good “American story” - 4th of July toasts.
“I give the U. S. bounded on the North by British Columbia, on 1 South by the Gulf of Mexico, on the East by the Atlantic and on 1 West by 1 Pacific.” 2-“I give the U. S. bounded on 1 N. by 1 N. Pole, on 1 S. by 1 S. Pole, on 1 East by 1 Rising Sun, and 1 W. by the Setting Sun” (great applause) 3 -“And I give the U.S., bounded on 1 N. by 1 Aurora Borealis, on 1 S. by 1 Precession of the Equinoxes, on 1 E. by Primeval Chaos, and on 1 W. by the Day of Judgment.”
Walked on the hill. Called on Mrs. Ross. Zangwill genial and nice.
[p093.b]
